  "id": "COMPOUND:15387 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound (1S,13S,16S,18R)-18-methoxy-12,15-dimethyl-5,7-dioxa-12,15-diazapentacyclo[11.7.0.01,16.02,10.04,8]icosa-2,4(8),9,19-tetraen-14-one and FaDu, as it is identified as a target of multiple enzymes in the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family. These enzymes are involved in metabolic processes that are often associated with cellular signaling and redox regulation. The compound's interaction with FaDu is supported by multiple pathways, including direct targeting by Erysimoside and (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, which are also part of the SDR family. This suggests that the compound may act through a common mechanism involving SDR family members, potentially modulating cellular processes that are critical for FaDu function. The evidence points to a role in metabolic pathways that are relevant to the biological activity of FaDu, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
